<section>
    <h2>Runtime DPR Access</h2>

    <p>unit.gl automatically injects the device pixel ratio as a CSS custom property, enabling dynamic density-aware
        calculations in CSS:</p>

    <div class="code-block"><pre><code><span class="comment">/* Available CSS custom properties */</span>
        :root {
        --dpr: 2; <span class="comment">/* Current device pixel ratio */</span>
        --dpr-inverse: 0.5; <span class="comment">/* 1 / DPR for inverse calculations */</span>
        }

        <span class="comment">/* Use in calculations */</span>
        .hairline {
        border-width: calc(1px * var(--dpr-inverse)); <span class="comment">/* True 1px on any display */</span>
        }

        .icon {
        <span class="comment">/* Scale based on density */</span>
        transform: scale(var(--dpr-inverse));
        }</code></pre></div>

    <div class="alert">
        <p class="alert__title">Note</p>
        <p>The <code>--dpr</code> variable updates automatically when moving windows between displays with different
            densities.</p>
    </div>
</section>
